# Keep everything LF in the working tree on every platform.
#
# This exists because of a Windows CI failure that looked like an upstream
# problem and was not. Git for Windows converts to CRLF on checkout, so the
# .patch files in THIS repo arrived with CRLF line endings while the upstream
# tree they apply to was LF. Every hunk failed with "does not apply".
#
# Both sides have to agree: bootstrap.sh clones upstream with autocrlf off, and
# this keeps our own patches and scripts from being rewritten under us.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Patches are byte-exact by nature — never let git touch them at all.
*.patch -text

# Shell scripts must keep LF or the shebang line breaks under bash.
*.sh text eol=lf
